WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.801 align:start size:3% position:97% line:0%
♪

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:04.771
(speaker #1):
Light and truth.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:08.742
(speaker #2):
That's our motto.
That's our tradition.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start position:0%
A tradition spoken...

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.481 align:start position:0%
...by the voices of
past Yale graduates.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:16.483
[Rising string music]

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:20.020 align:start position:0%
It is important for all of us to
appreciate where we come from

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.123
and how that history has really
shaped us

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:26.059
in ways that we
might not understand.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.995 align:start position:0%
With your knowledge,
may you always be curious.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.764
With your experience,

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:33.233
may you always remember
where you started.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.202 align:start position:0%
The distance between
number one and number two

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.971 align:start position:0%
is always a constant.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.672
If you want to improve the
organization,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.207
you have to improve yourself

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.910
and the organization gets
pulled up with you.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.813
Yale has a
long and honored tradition

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:50.450 align:start position:0%
of many people who have
made big changes to nursing

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.185 align:start position:0%
and the profession.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.287
They are the ones that
created the tradition,

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.590
but you are the
keepers of the flame.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.592
I have been fighting
climate change for two decades,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.495 align:start position:0%
and people often ask me
how I remain hopeful

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.031 align:start position:0%
in the face of extreme weather
and grim forecasts.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.734
The answer is simple:
I see countless solutions

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.136
spreading across the nation
and across the world.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.271 align:start position:0%
Our view of nature

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.673 align:start position:0%
will influence the way
we treat nature,

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.241
and our view of human nature

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.778
will affect our understanding
of human responsibility.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:21.981
If we only are looking for parts
of ourselves in others,

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start position:0%
we will never really see
or listen fully,

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:28.188
and we will never really see all
of the aspects of a person.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.790
Because we are always
more than one thing.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.160
We don’t have to tamp down
parts of ourselves or others.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.330 align:start position:0%
No matter where you are from,
your dreams are valid.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.898
You have to have conviction

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.201
and completely question
everything and anything you do.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.637
No matter how much you study,
no matter how much you know,

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.439 align:end position:100%
the side of your brain that
has the smarts

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.541 align:end position:100%
won’t necessarily help you
in making art.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start position:0%
Empathy is choosing to
see ourselves in another

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.712 size:75% position:38%
despite our differences.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.914
It’s recognizing that
the same humanity,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.351
the same desire for meaning,
fulfillment and security,

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:01.488
exists in each of us, even if
it’s expressed uniquely.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.223 size:78% position:39%
Don’t settle for average.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.858
Bring your best to the moment.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:07.527
Then, whether it
fails or succeeds,

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.762
at least you know you
gave it all you had.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.564 align:start position:0%
If you do your best
when you’re young

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.100 align:start position:0%
and try the hardest to fulfil
your dreams

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.604 size:84% position:42%
but you don't succeed, then
at least when you reach 80,

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start position:0%
you can say, I didn’t succeed as
I wanted, but I know I tried.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.245 align:start position:0%
We need you to help us
create the new normal.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.147
Utilize your
privileged education

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.448
and your flexible position

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.583
to propel us towards
a healthier society.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.452 align:start position:0%
Don’t let anyone tell you
how to live.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.587 align:start position:0%
You create your
own world now.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.489
The world needs you to
create something new.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.058
The gift my parents gave me,
the gift of no limits,

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.561
we need to pass along
to the next generation.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.061 line:92%
So...

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:42.428
So...

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:42.896
So...

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.130 line:92%
Class of 2021...

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.231
Class of 2021...

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.833
Class of 2021...

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.202
(all speakers:)
What will our voice be?

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:54.307
[piano music] ♪♪

